🦉 Owlyshield — Linux Installation Guide

Owlyshield is an open-source EDR (Endpoint Detection & Response) framework written in Rust.
It analyzes process and file activity to detect intrusions, C2 beacons, and fileless malware.
This guide provides a step-by-step Linux installation process to build and deploy Owlyshield from source.

⚙️ Prerequisites

Ensure you are running:
- Ubuntu / Debian / Fedora / CentOS / Arch (Linux x86_64)

Root or sudo access

Required dependencies:

git

curl

systemd

build-essential or equivalent

rustc and cargo (Rust toolchain)



🚀 Quick Install

Run the following in your terminal:

- curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RoyRonik/Owlyshield/main/install_owlyshield.sh -o install_owlyshield.sh
- chmod +x install_owlyshield.sh
- sudo ./install_owlyshield.sh




🧰 Installation Script

Save the following as install_owlyshield.sh (already referenced above):

#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

# ----------------------------------------
# Owlyshield - Linux Installation Script
# Author: Roy Ronik
# Repo: https://github.com/RoyRonik/Owlyshield
# ----------------------------------------

REPO_URL="https://github.com/RoyRonik/Owlyshield.git"
INSTALL_DIR="/opt/owlyshield"
BIN_NAME="owlyshield"
SERVICE_FILE="/etc/systemd/system/owlyshield.service"
LOG_FILE="/var/log/owlyshield.log"

log_info()   { echo -e "\033[1;34m[INFO]\033[0m  $*"; }
log_warn()   { echo -e "\033[1;33m[WARN]\033[0m  $*"; }
log_error()  { echo -e "\033[1;31m[ERROR]\033[0m $*" >&2; }

log_info "🦉 Starting Owlyshield installation..."

# ----------------------------------------
# Check prerequisites
# ----------------------------------------

for cmd in git curl systemctl; do
    if ! command -v "$cmd" &>/dev/null; then
        log_warn "Missing dependency: $cmd"
        MISSING=1
    fi
done

if [ -n "${MISSING:-}" ]; then
    log_info "Installing missing packages..."
    if [ -f /etc/debian_version ]; then
        sudo apt update
        sudo apt install -y git curl build-essential
    elif [ -f /etc/redhat-release ]; then
        sudo yum install -y git curl gcc make
    elif [ -f /etc/arch-release ]; then
        sudo pacman -Sy --noconfirm git curl base-devel
    else
        log_warn "Unsupported distro — please install dependencies manually."
    fi
fi

if ! command -v cargo &>/dev/null; then
    log_info "Installing Rust toolchain..."
    curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh -s -- -y
    source "$HOME/.cargo/env"
fi

# ----------------------------------------
# Clone or update repo
# ----------------------------------------
if [ -d "$INSTALL_DIR" ]; then
    log_info "Updating existing Owlyshield repo..."
    cd "$INSTALL_DIR"
    git pull --ff-only
else
    log_info "Cloning Owlyshield repository..."
    sudo git clone "$REPO_URL" "$INSTALL_DIR"
    sudo chown -R "$(whoami)" "$INSTALL_DIR"
fi

# ----------------------------------------
# Build from source
# ----------------------------------------
log_info "Building Owlyshield (release mode)..."
cd "$INSTALL_DIR"
cargo build --release

# ----------------------------------------
# Install binary
# ----------------------------------------
BUILD_BIN="./target/release/$BIN_NAME"
if [ ! -x "$BUILD_BIN" ]; then
    log_error "Build failed — binary not found: $BUILD_BIN"
    exit 1
fi

sudo cp "$BUILD_BIN" /usr/local/bin/
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/$BIN_NAME

# ----------------------------------------
# Configure logging
# ----------------------------------------
sudo mkdir -p "$(dirname "$LOG_FILE")"
sudo touch "$LOG_FILE"
sudo chmod 644 "$LOG_FILE"

# ----------------------------------------
# Create systemd service
# ----------------------------------------
if [ ! -f "$SERVICE_FILE" ]; then
    log_info "Creating systemd service..."
    sudo bash -c "cat > $SERVICE_FILE" <<EOF
[Unit]
Description=Owlyshield EDR Service
After=network.target

[Service]
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/$BIN_NAME
WorkingDirectory=$INSTALL_DIR
StandardOutput=append:$LOG_FILE
StandardError=append:$LOG_FILE
Restart=always
User=root

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
EOF
    sudo systemctl daemon-reload
    sudo systemctl enable owlyshield
fi

log_info "✅ Installation complete!"
log_info "Start service: sudo systemctl start owlyshield"
log_info "View logs: tail -f $LOG_FILE"



🧩 Post-Installation

After installation, you can:

Start the service:
- sudo systemctl start owlyshield

Check service status:
- sudo systemctl status owlyshield

Stop the service:
- sudo systemctl stop owlyshield

View logs:
- sudo tail -f /var/log/owlyshield.log



🧼 Uninstall:

To completely remove Owlyshield:

- sudo systemctl stop owlyshield
- sudo systemctl disable owlyshield
- sudo rm -f /usr/local/bin/owlyshield
- sudo rm -rf /opt/owlyshield
sudo rm -f /etc/systemd/system/owlyshield.service
sudo rm -f /var/log/owlyshield.log
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
